in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/pact
in @epistemologic/pact/bilateral
in @epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace
in @apply_h
in @fractal
in @fractal/shard

# @epistemologic/normalization/alpha_reduce — alpha-normalization at
# AST altitude. Renames all bound parameter names to de Bruijn indices
# (`_@0`, `_@1`, ...) so that two shards differing only in parameter
# names hash identically. Carrier refs at `@X` position are NOT alpha-
# renamed (they are content-addressed refs, not binders; alpha-
# invariance would break identity resolution).
#
# Per Alex 2026-08-11 Q1 concur-with-Mara-lean: LAND ALPHA-NORMALIZATION
# for parameter names only. Substrate-honest closure of Dhall parity
# (Dhall pairs beta with alpha per standard/alpha-normalization.md);
# small delta (~50 LOC at rust/ altitude); avoids the trap of hashing
# accidental parameter-name variation.
#
# Reed Fire E M-E3-REVISED landing per Mara canonical spec 5ad8528
# §8 [ALEX-Q1] Mara-lean + Alex 2026-08-11 concur.
#
# === What alpha-normalization does at mirror substrate ===
#
# Two shards that differ only in parameter names should hash identically:
#
#   Shard A: `beta_reduce(ast: ref, rule: ref) -> ref { \ }`
#   Shard B: `beta_reduce(tree: ref, r: ref) -> ref { \ }`
#
# Alpha-normal form:
#
#   Both: `beta_reduce(_@0: ref, _@1: ref) -> ref { \ }`
#
# Same de Bruijn index positions; same alpha-normal AST; same OID.
#
# Carrier refs at `@X` position are NOT renamed:
#
#   `focus ast_reduction` → `focus ast_reduction` (unchanged)
#
# `ast_reduction` is a type-reference, not a bound parameter; alpha-
# invariance would break identity resolution at the @mirror/store
# lookup.
#
# === Prior art ===
#
# Dhall standard/alpha-normalization.md verbatim: *"if two expressions
# are α-equivalent then they will be identical after α-normalization"*.
# Formal notation `t₀ ↦ t₁`. de Bruijn indices per de Bruijn 1972.
# Standard construction from Barendregt 1984.
#
# === Composition ===
#
# Read-path pipeline position:
#
#   ... |> beta_normalize |> alpha_reduce |> compute_content_oid ...
#
# alpha_reduce runs AFTER beta_normalize (per Dhall pipeline convention;
# some beta-reductions may introduce new parameters or eliminate old
# ones; alpha-normalization runs last to canonicalize the final form).
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]
# [[feedback-rust-delivers-primitives-substrate-delivers-composition]]
#   — alpha_reduce lands as shard body composing over apply_h::act +
#   Fold5 primitives; NO new Rust module.
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] — body `\`-obligation-blocked; Reed
#   Fire E M-E3.5-REVISED discharges at rust/ altitude via apply_h::act.
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] — typed `ast: ref`.
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/normalization/alpha_reduce.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/normalization/alpha_reduce` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/practice/mara-2026-08-10-beta-normal-ast-content-addressing
source @arxiv/practice/wolf-2026-08-11-q1-concur-alpha-normalization-parameter-names
source @arxiv/lambda/de-bruijn-1972-nameless-dummies
source @arxiv/lambda/barendregt-1984-lambda-calculus-syntax-semantics
source @arxiv/topology/dhall-lang-standard-alpha-normalization

prism @epistemologic/normalization/alpha_reduce {
  focus alpha_reduction
  project alpha_reduction
  split alpha_reduction
  shift alpha_reduction
  settle alpha_reduction
}

# === alpha_reduction carrier ===
type alpha_reduction = {
  ast_pre:            ref,
  parameter_renaming: ref,
  ast_post:           ref,
  witness:            ref,
}

# === alpha_reduce action ===
#
# Renames all bound parameter names in the AST to de Bruijn indices.
# Preserves carrier refs at `@X` positions (they are content-addressed
# refs, not binders).
#
# Body `\`-obligation-blocked; Reed Fire E M-E3.5-REVISED extends
# apply_h::act dispatch with alpha_reduce sentinel arm.
#
# `requires well_formed(ast)`: input must be syntactically valid
# (delegates to @epistemologic/normalization/beta_reduce.well_formed).
# `ensures parameter_names_are_de_bruijn(result)`: all parameter
# occurrences in the output AST are of shape `_@<index>`.
alpha_reduce(ast: ref) -> ref
requires well_formed(ast)
ensures parameter_names_are_de_bruijn(result)
{ \ }

# === parameter_names_are_de_bruijn — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Rice-safe byte-check: all bound parameter occurrences in the AST
# match the pattern `_@\d+` (de Bruijn index form). Reads only byte-
# visible state (parameter-name tokens in AST); no semantics.
#
# Sentinel: `parameters=de-bruijn-indexed`.
bilateral parameter_names_are_de_bruijn_pact {
  sentinel "parameters=de-bruijn-indexed"
  arity 1
}
parameter_names_are_de_bruijn(ast: ref) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/normalization/alpha_reduce
out alpha_reduction
out alpha_reduce
out parameter_names_are_de_bruijn
out parameter_names_are_de_bruijn_pact
